  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "No chapter describes its appearance.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s variant human alliance has become a huge threat to Eastern Sea’s super forces, and a recent defeat has raised their wariness. Forced by that pressure, the clans gather in a hall.",
      "chapters": [
        2074
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "reg_eastern_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qi Sea Ancestor sets three tasks: an alliance storage that every clan must supply with resources, Immortal Gu recipes, and immortal killer moves; a contribution board and mission board so merits are known; and mutual help, including allying to remove a traitor. The immortals agree that without this the Righteous Qi Alliance would exist only in name. The first group discussion covers exchange of true inheritances and communication of geniuses across clans, negotiation to recover captured Gu Immortals, and contacting Heavenly Court in the alliance’s name. News of that stretch spreads until Eastern Sea has split into two large alliances in confrontation.",
      "chapters": [
        2074
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qi_sea_ancestor",
        "sys_gu_recipe",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To resolve an ant plague, Qi Sea Ancestor requires the clans to contribute their true inheritances, with the contribution board as the promised reward and compensation. Hua clan, Nan Gong clan, Xie clan, Su clan, and others take inheritances out. The board, which had few names, lengthens and the ranking competition intensifies. Qi Sea Ancestor assesses the value of each inheritance. The contribution of true inheritances becomes a competition and a political conflict between the clans, while Qi Sea Ancestor, from the main seat, is the biggest beneficiary.",
      "chapters": [
        2105
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "true-inheritance-drive",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_hua_clan",
        "fac_nan_gong_clan",
        "fac_xie_clan",
        "fac_su_clan"
      ]
    }
